.TH SDL_PathType 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_PathType \- Types of filesystem entries.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_filesystem.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_PathType
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_PATHTYPE_NONE,      /**< path does not exist */
.BI "    SDL_PATHTYPE_FILE,      /**< a normal file */
.BI "    SDL_PATHTYPE_DIRECTORY, /**< a directory */
.BI "    SDL_PATHTYPE_OTHER      /**< something completely different like a device node (not a symlink, those are always followed) */
.BI "} SDL_PathType;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that there may be other sorts of items on a filesystem: devices, named pipes, etc\[char46] They are currently reported as
.BR SDL_PATHTYPE_OTHER \[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_PathInfo (3type)
